    "rank": 1776943407.0,
    "content": "Are you looking out for a little set of desktop PC speakers on a tight budget? If so, you may be interested in this latest Woot offer that brings the price of a set of\nRazer Nommo 2.0 speakers to a bargain $69.99\n. This saves you a substantial $40 off the original $109.99 price tag. Razer is well known for making PC peripherals, which include speakers, keyboards, headsets, and, of course, mice. Razer products often command high prices, especially direct from Razer, but there are some deals to be found from other retailers that stock Razer products.\n●\nGrab this deal at Woot\nThe Razer Nommo speakers are a simple 2.0 configuration, with no added subwoofer, so don't expect a tsunami of bass. But this can be a good thing, especially if you're going to be using these speakers in an environment that doesn't need to hear thumping sub-bass rumbling through the property. Making a small set of speakers like this is ideal for some PC or console gaming in the bedroom, or even a dorm room at college, where you want to limit disturbances.\nThe speakers themselves are attractive little cans hoisted on small stands with 3\" woven glass fiber drivers mounted in the front and a bass port at the rear, to add a little kick to the bass frequencies. Volume and bass controls are mounted on the right speaker's stand and let you pump the bass (as much as you can on a 2.0 set of speakers) with its automatic gain control. These are older Razer speakers and have been replaced by newer models on the Razer store, which is one of the reasons these speakers are much cheaper now.\nA downside to these speakers for PC use is a lack of USB connectivity. You need to connect these Razer Nommo speakers to your PC via a 3.5mm to 3.5mm cable to an appropriate audio port on either the rear IO of your motherboard or the headphone jack of your PC's case. Yes, there are newer variants of these speakers, including the Razer Nommo V2 2.1, which comes with a subwoofer and is our pick for the\nbest 2.1 gaming speakers\n. But for just $69.99, these speakers are a great little deal, while stocks last, or time runs out on this limited Woot offer.\nIf you're looking for more savings, check out our\nBest PC Hardware deals\nfor a range of products, or dive\ndeeper\ninto\nour\nspecialized\nSSD and Storage Deals,\nHard Drive Deals\n,\nGaming Monitor Deals\n,\nGraphics Card Deals\n,\nGaming Chair\n,\nBest Wi-Fi Routers\n,\nBest Motherboard,\nor\nCPU Deals\npages\n.",
